======================================================================================================================
JOINT CALIBRATION -- held out, copula against independence
======================================================================================================================
  For every pair of levels (a, b) on the 5 x 5 grid, the event
  {MAE <= Q_MAE(a) and MFE <= Q_MFE(b)}. Actual frequency against the
  copula's C(a,b) and independence's a*b. gap = mean |actual - predicted|
  over the 25 pairs, in pp. cop-ind is PAIRED on identical rows and day
  resamples: negative = the copula describes the joint law better.
  'dep only' plugs the ACTUAL held-out marginal frequencies into the
  copula -- a diagnostic that removes marginal miscalibration and scores
  the dependence structure alone. Point estimate only; it uses held-out
  marginals, so it is not a forecast.

